# Treat generated binary office/PDF output as opaque binary for diff purposes.
# Without this, `git diff`/`git diff --cached` can hang trying to compute a textual/binary diff
# on some PDFs (observed 2026-09-18 on a preschool-teaching Nota Pembelajaran PDF — reproduced
# directly with `git diff --cached -- <file>` timing out with zero output; root cause not fully
# isolated, but marking these extensions `-diff` makes git skip diff computation entirely, which
# is also just correct practice for generated binary artefacts).
# This does NOT reduce the repo's secret-scan pre-commit hook coverage: that hook only scans
# `+`-added TEXT LINES from `git diff --cached`, and binary files never produce those lines
# regardless of this attribute — their source .md/.docx files are still scanned as text.
*.pdf -diff
*.docx -diff
*.xlsx -diff
*.pptx -diff
*.doc -diff
*.xls -diff
*.ppt -diff
